WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:12.138
Hi! We breathe with our lungs. But fish live in water, and plants don't even have mouths. So how do they get oxygen? Let's compare!

2
00:00:12.288 --> 00:00:19.290
Humans exchange gases in the lungs. We take in oxygen from the air and give out carbon dioxide.

3
00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:28.818
The exchange happens in the many tiny air sacs of the lungs. Oxygen enters the blood, and carbon dioxide leaves it.

4
00:00:28.968 --> 00:00:33.858
Fish don't have lungs. They exchange gases using gills.

5
00:00:34.008 --> 00:00:41.082
A fish opens its mouth to let water in. The water flows over the gills and out through the gill openings.

6
00:00:41.232 --> 00:00:49.650
There is oxygen dissolved in the water. The gills take this oxygen into the blood, and pass carbon dioxide out into the water.

7
00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:55.242
Gills have lots of blood vessels, which is why they look red.

8
00:00:55.392 --> 00:01:02.154
Plant leaves have many tiny openings, mostly on the underside. Air moves in and out through them.

9
00:01:02.304 --> 00:01:08.730
Plants respire too. Day and night, they take in oxygen and give out carbon dioxide.

10
00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:17.514
When there is light, plants also make food. To do this, they take in carbon dioxide and give out oxygen.

11
00:01:17.664 --> 00:01:22.506
Let's sum up. Humans use lungs to get oxygen from the air.

12
00:01:22.656 --> 00:01:26.490
Fish use gills to get oxygen dissolved in water.

13
00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:32.778
Plants use tiny openings on their leaves to exchange gases with the air.

14
00:01:32.928 --> 00:01:40.554
Watch out! Many pupils say plants only give out oxygen and never need it themselves. That's wrong!

15
00:01:40.704 --> 00:01:46.482
Like all living things, plants respire. They take in oxygen day and night.

16
00:01:46.632 --> 00:01:53.946
It's just that in light, the oxygen they give out while making food is more than the oxygen they use.

17
00:01:54.096 --> 00:02:02.466
Your turn! Where do fish get their oxygen from? Pause and think.

18
00:02:02.616 --> 00:02:10.122
Fish use their gills to take in oxygen that is dissolved in the water. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:10.272 --> 00:02:19.770
Another one! On which side of a leaf are most of the tiny openings? Pause and think.

20
00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:25.554
Mostly on the underside of the leaf. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:25.704 --> 00:02:35.514
Last one! At night when there is no light, which gas do plants take in? Pause and think.

22
00:02:35.664 --> 00:02:43.290
Oxygen. Plants don't make food at night, but they still respire. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:58.770
Remember: humans use lungs, fish use gills, and plants use tiny openings on their leaves to exchange gases. All living things respire. In light, plants also take in carbon dioxide and give out oxygen to make food.

24
00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:03.882
Go and watch how a fish in a tank opens its mouth!

